# Day 11 – Python EV ADAS Dashboard

## Objective

Developed a Python-based graphical dashboard to monitor the Real-Time EV Dashboard and ADAS system.

The dashboard receives telemetry data from the STM32 Blue Pill through UART and displays the vehicle and ADAS parameters graphically.

## Features

- Real-time UART telemetry monitoring
- EV speedometer
- Battery SOC indicator
- Estimated driving range
- Motor torque display
- Motor temperature monitoring
- Accelerator and brake status
- Front obstacle distance
- Left and right obstacle distance
- Time to Collision (TTC)
- Collision warning
- Blind Spot Detection
- Alarm priority
- Fault status
- Speed history graph
- UART connection status
- Demo mode without hardware

## UART Communication

The dashboard communicates with the STM32 through a serial port.

Example:

```text
python dashboard.py --port COM3
